a "which of these have you used" group ticks only what is on the CV
a blank customAnswers entry is a warning, not an error
a certification the CV does not contain is not claimed
a configured skill still answers with its number
a named technology never borrows the total-experience figure
a resume file input is filled from config.resumePath
a resume summary contradicting config.experienceYears is flagged
a tenure question is not answered with total career experience
an opt-in fallback fills unconfigured skill years, capped at total experience
known candidate facts are answered without an API call
known skill-specific experience uses configured skill years
resume-answers never leaves a yes/no field blank (no AI, all local/CV-based)
resume-profile detects skills mentioned in the CV
salary reaches the field with the unit conversion applied
short numeric answers do not falsely substring-match option text
skill claims come from the CV — never from an optimistic default
technologies that ARE on the CV are not needlessly denied
the shipped config passes with no errors
valid search settings pass
yes/no skill questions are unaffected by the quantity guard
